    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d578">

                <pb facs="0602" n="590" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg590"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">859.85/10–345: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Denmark</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Davis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-10-03T18:00:00+01:00">October 3, 1945—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:23 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>461. Kauffmann seemed optimistic regarding prospect for early settlement Danish
                    claim for ship turned over the US Government since he had succeeded in getting
                    Prime Minister,<anchor n="83" xml:id="d578-f1"/> other officials and
                    representatives shipping lines with single exception of A. P. Moller,<anchor
                        n="84" xml:id="d578-f2"/> in agreement as to Danish position. He hopes that
                    Moller will not be too difficult and satisfactory settlement can be effected
                    soon after his return US. I refrained from discussing details with Kauffmann but
                    gained impression that he is more objective about matter than he was when he
                    discussed it with me first in Washington and later in London during May. He
                    feels the importance of prompt settlement for both political and economic
                    reasons. It is hoped Department will keep Legation informed of progress of
                    negotiations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d578-f1" n="83" xml:id="d578-f1-content">
                <p>Vilhelm Buhl.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d578-f2" n="84" xml:id="d578-f2-content">
                <p>Arnold Peter Moller, managing owner of the Svendborg Steamship Company and the
                    1912 Steamship Company.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
